  "body": "In https://github.com/whatwg/url/issues/77, I was surprised that `.` was such a special case. It is indeed in Firefox 44, but in Chromium 48 other characters are also percent-decoded: `-`, `_`, `~`, and ASCII alpha-numerics. (I don’t have other browsers to test right now.)\n\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=3878\n\nIt may be worth testing other URL components too.\n",
